damaged_code:
```rust
struct Account {
    balance: i64,
    alerts_sent: usize,
}

impl Account {
    pub fn get_balance_and_report_overdraft(&mut self) -> i64 {
        if self.balance < 0 {
            self.alerts_sent += 1; // Side effect!
            send_alert();
        }
        self.balance
    }
}
```

counterexample:
A pure query returning values without side effects, and a separate command that mutates state and returns nothing (`()`):
```rust
impl Account {
    pub fn balance(&self) -> i64 {
        self.balance
    }
    pub fn trigger_overdraft_alerts(&mut self) {
        if self.balance < 0 {
            self.alerts_sent += 1;
            send_alert();
        }
    }
}
```

fix:
Split the side-effecting query into a read-only query method and a state-modifying command method.
```rust
// Caller must execute sequentially:
account.trigger_overdraft_alerts();
let bal = account.balance();
```
